  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "DnsResource::getDataLength",
    "file": "PcapPlusPlus/Packet++/src/DnsResource.cpp",
    "description": "Heap out-of-bounds read in DNS resource length parsing due to an incorrect boundary check. `getDataLength()` reads a 16-bit `dataLength` field at `getRawData() + sizeToRead`, but its guard uses `m_OffsetInLayer + sizeToRead >= m_DnsLayer->m_DataLen - 1`, which can be bypassed/overflowed and is not a robust 'need 2 bytes available' check. As a result, `DnsLayer::parseResources()` calls `newResource->getSize()` (via `DnsResource.h`) on truncated/malformed DNS records and triggers a 2-byte read past the packet buffer.",
    "conditions": "From the fuzzer path (`FuzzTarget`), attacker-controlled packet bytes are parsed as UDP/DNS. DNS header counters cause `DnsLayer::parseResources()` to instantiate a `DnsResource` near the end of the DNS payload. If the resource header is truncated so fewer than 2 bytes remain for the RDLENGTH field, `getDataLength()` still dereferences `uint16_t` at the end of buffer, causing ASan heap-buffer-overflow read. Data flow: raw pcap -> `Packet::setRawPacket` -> `UdpLayer::parseNextLayer` -> `DnsLayer::parseResources` -> `DnsResource::getSize` -> `DnsResource::getDataLength` crash."
  },
